  "story": "The phone's wall clock reads two seconds behind the laptop's. It sees the laptop's write to part 5, then, offline, writes part 5 again. A plain wall clock would let the laptop's older write win; the hybrid clock carries the laptop's time into the phone, so the phone's later edit wins. On part 6 both write in the same millisecond of hybrid time and the counter decides.",
